The nchan module turns nginx into a publish and subscribe server.  Clients
subscribe over websocket, EventSource, long polling or plain HTTP, and
messages published to a channel reach all of its subscribers.

Messages can be kept in shared memory or in Redis, which lets several
servers share the same channels.  Channel state and subscriber counts are
available over an HTTP interface.

This port only installs the module sources.  The module itself is built by
the nginx ports when their HTTP_PUSH option is enabled.
